<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
<title>Data-Cleaning Tool · usage and demo run</title>
<meta name="description" content="A command-line tool that cleans messy CSV and Excel exports reproducibly from a YAML profile, with a rejects file and an HTML report. Demo run on invented survey data.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="kit/fonts/fonts.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="kit/tokens.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="kit/base.css">
<script src="kit/theme-boot.js"></script>
<style>
main{display:grid;gap:var(--space-7);min-width:0}
main>section{display:grid;gap:var(--space-4);min-width:0}
.lead{max-width:68ch;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--fs-lg)}
.points{display:grid;gap:var(--space-2);padding-left:1.2em}
.points li::marker{color:var(--accent)}
.prose{max-width:72ch}
.term{margin:0;padding:var(--space-3) var(--space-4);overflow-x:auto;font-variant-ligatures:none;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);background:var(--surface-2);font-size:var(--fs-xs);line-height:1.55;tab-size:4}
.term--cmd{color:var(--text);font-size:var(--fs-sm)}
.term--cmd::before{content:"$ ";content:"$ "/"";color:var(--accent)}
.stream{display:grid;gap:var(--space-1);min-width:0}
.step{display:grid;gap:var(--space-3);min-width:0}
.step h3{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:var(--space-2)}
.note{color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--fs-sm)}
.pf-table tbody tr td.is-changed{position:relative;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 18%,var(--surface));box-shadow:inset 0 -2px 0 var(--accent)}
.pf-table tbody th{color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);text-transform:none}
.legend{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--space-2);color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--fs-sm)}
.legend__swatch{display:inline-block;width:1.4em;height:1em;border-radius:3px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 18%,var(--surface));box-shadow:inset 0 -2px 0 var(--accent)}
.files{display:grid;gap:var(--space-2);padding:0;list-style:none}
.files li{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--space-1) var(--space-3);padding:var(--space-2) var(--space-3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);background:var(--surface)}
.files span{color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:var(--fs-xs)}
.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:var(--space-2)}
</style>
</head>
<body class="pf-has-banner">
<aside class="pf-banner" aria-label="Demo notice"><span>Demo with invented data for a fictional company</span><a href="{{ repo }}">Source code</a></aside>
<div class="pf-page">
<header class="pf-header">
  <a class="pf-brand" href="./"><span class="pf-brand__mark" aria-hidden="true">HH</span>Data-Cleaning Tool</a>
  <nav class="pf-header__nav" aria-label="Sections"><a href="#install">Install</a><a href="#demo">Demo run</a><a href="#before-after">Before and after</a><a href="#files">Files</a><a href="#exit-codes">Exit codes</a></nav>
  <div class="pf-header__tools"><span id="theme"></span></div>
</header>
<main>
<section aria-labelledby="top">
  <h1 id="top">Data-Cleaning Tool</h1>
  <p class="lead">Cleans messy CSV and Excel exports reproducibly from a YAML profile, with a rejects file and an HTML report. Version {{ version }}, shown here on an invented survey export of a fictional panel research company.</p>
  <ul class="points">
    <li>Reads CSV and Excel the same way every time: encoding and delimiter sniffing, header offsets, footer rows, several sheets, short and malformed records.</li>
    <li>Normalises headers to snake_case and cleans text: Unicode form, invisible characters, whitespace, null tokens, case and value maps.</li>
    <li>Converts types with German and English number and date formats; a value that does not parse is rejected, never guessed.</li>
    <li>Removes exact and key duplicates (fuzzy matching as an option), fills missing values per column and checks ranges, patterns and allowed values.</li>
    <li>Writes the cleaned file (CSV, Excel or Parquet), every removed row with its reason, and a JSON and HTML report with before and after statistics.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--primary" href="demo/report.html">Open the cleaning report</a>
    <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--ghost" href="{{ repo }}">Source code and documentation</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <h2 id="install-title">Install and run</h2>
  <p class="prose">Install the command from the release wheel with <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/">uv</a>, extras included:</p>
  <pre class="term term--cmd"><code>uv tool install "data-cleaning-tool[fuzzy,parquet] @ {{ repo }}/releases/download/v{{ version }}/data_cleaning_tool-{{ version }}-py3-none-any.whl"</code></pre>
  <p class="prose">Or work from a clone, which also has the fixtures and profiles used below:</p>
  <pre class="term term--cmd"><code>git clone {{ repo }}.git &amp;&amp; cd data-cleaning-tool &amp;&amp; uv sync --all-extras</code></pre>
  <p class="prose">In a clone, put <code>uv run</code> in front of each <code>clean-data</code> command. The extras are optional: <code>fuzzy</code> (rapidfuzz) for fuzzy de-duplication, <code>parquet</code> (pyarrow) for Parquet output.</p>
</section>

<section id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
  <h2 id="demo-title">Demo run on the survey fixture</h2>
  <p class="prose">Four commands on <code>fixtures/01_survey_export_de.csv</code>, a German survey export with {{ records_read }} records, recorded with version {{ version }}. Standard output carries results only; logs and the explain text go to standard error.</p>
  <div class="pf-grid" style="--min:140px">
  {% for label, value in counts %}
    <div class="pf-kpi"><span class="pf-kpi__label pf-label">{{ label }}</span><span class="pf-kpi__value">{{ value }}</span></div>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% for step in steps %}
  <article class="step" id="step-{{ step.key }}" aria-labelledby="step-{{ step.key }}-title">
    <h3 id="step-{{ step.key }}-title"><span class="pf-label">{{ loop.index }} of {{ steps|length }}</span>{{ step.title }}</h3>
    <pre class="term term--cmd"><code>{{ step.command }}</code></pre>
    {% if step.note %}
    <p class="note">{{ step.note }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if step.stdout %}
    <div class="stream"><span class="pf-label">stdout</span><pre class="term" tabindex="0"><code>{{ step.stdout }}</code></pre></div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if step.stderr %}
    <div class="stream"><span class="pf-label">stderr</span><pre class="term" tabindex="0"><code>{{ step.stderr }}</code></pre></div>
    {% endif %}
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="before-after" aria-labelledby="before-after-title">
  <h2 id="before-after-title">Before and after: the first {{ records|length }} records</h2>
  <p class="prose">Values as read (after header normalisation) and as written. Invisible characters are shown as escapes such as <code>&#92;u00a0</code>.</p>
  <p class="legend"><span class="legend__swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span>Tinted and underlined: the cell changed during cleaning.</p>
  <div class="pf-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="before-caption">
    <table class="pf-table">
      <caption id="before-caption">Before: as read</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">row</th>{% for name in names %}<th scope="col">{{ name }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for record in records %}
        <tr><th scope="row">{{ record.label }}</th>{% for cell in record.before %}<td>{{ cell.text }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="pf-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="after-caption">
    <table class="pf-table">
      <caption id="after-caption">After: as written to cleaned.csv</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">row</th><th scope="col">status</th>{% for name in names %}<th scope="col">{{ name }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for record in records %}
        <tr><th scope="row">{{ record.label }}</th><td>{{ record.status }}</td>{% for cell in record.after %}{% if cell.changed %}<td class="is-changed"><span class="pf-visually-hidden">changed: </span>{{ cell.text }}</td>{% else %}<td>{{ cell.text }}</td>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="files" aria-labelledby="files-title">
  <h2 id="files-title">Files of the demo run</h2>
  <ul class="files">
  {% for name, size in files %}
    <li><a href="demo/{{ name }}">{{ name }}</a><span>{{ size }}</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="note">CI rebuilds these files and this page with <code>tools/build_demo.py --check</code> and fails on any byte difference.</p>
</section>

<section id="exit-codes" aria-labelledby="exit-title">
  <h2 id="exit-title">Exit codes</h2>
  <div class="pf-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="exit-title">
    <table class="pf-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">exit</th><th scope="col">meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for code, meaning in exit_codes %}
        <tr><td class="pf-num">{{ code }}</td><td style="white-space:normal">{{ meaning }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
<footer class="pf-footer">
  <p>Rebuilt from memory as a demo. The original client's name and data are not used.</p>
  <p>Northgate Panel Research is a fictional company; every record is invented. <a href="{{ repo }}">Source code</a> under the MIT licence.</p>
</footer>
</div>
<script type="module">
import { mountBanner, mountThemeToggle } from './kit/kit.js';
mountBanner({ repoUrl: '{{ repo }}' });
mountThemeToggle(document.getElementById('theme'));
</script>
</body>
</html>
